    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0644" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg542"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Wilson to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-02-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 5,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Government yesterday withdrew Kongo annexation treaty from consideration of
                    Parliament, with statement that it proposed to submit a new project in lieu of
                    it. This, it is understood, will provide for suppression of the Domain of the
                    Crown, with equivalents to the King in the form of special civil list for
                    realizing the philanthropic, scientific, and other enterprises of the King in
                    Belgium and in the Kongo. The new treaty, if submitted as indicated, will be
                    adopted and will, in my judgment, afford a solution of the Kongo question
                    satisfactory to Belgian and international opinion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
